[{:adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-3312 "ADR-2607103900's own (is (= 25 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 26 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"3312\")))) alongside the twenty-five prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test", :adr/github-contents-api-outage-workaround "the usual gh api 'repos/com-junkawasaki/root/contents/90-docs/adr?ref=main' command used to freshly verify the next-available ADR id returned a transient GitHub 500 'Unicorn' error page (likely a response-size/timeout issue as the ADR directory has grown large). Worked around by using the Git Trees API instead (git/trees/main -> 90-docs subtree -> adr subtree), which returned the directory listing successfully and confirmed '2607104000' as the next available id. No change to the fresh-verification discipline itself, just an alternate API path for the same check", :adr/related ["2607103900-cloud-itonami-buildingcleaning-8121-blueprint" "2607103700-cloud-itonami-rollingstock-3020-blueprint" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607104000", :adr/next-steps-3312 "cloud-itonami-isic-3312 joins the twenty-five prior fresh-blueprint picks as a twenty-sixth candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass. '8129' remains explicitly deferred for a future build requiring a narrow scoping pass against cloud-itonami-unspsc-73's existing industrial-cleaning coverage. '3313' (repair of electronic and optical equipment) remains available as a low-friction sibling pick. The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (514 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)", :adr/reuse-manufacturing-lifecycle-shape-3312 "the registry's own pre-existing :operating-states for '3312' (:spec :design :produce :inspect :package :audit) matches the SAME manufacturing-lifecycle shape used for rollingstockops/3020, meddeviceops/2660 and basicchemops/2011 -- this build reuses it verbatim, adapted for repair-authority/certification concerns", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 25, :spec 515, :total 646}", :adr/explicit-scope-note-3312 "the README's own 'Scope note' section directly names cloud-itonami-isic-3020 and cloud-itonami-unspsc-73, and explains the repair-vs-manufacture and repair-vs-cleaning distinctions with specific certification-regime citations, matching the discipline established repeatedly this window", :adr/registry-field-replacement-3312 "the existing '3312' registry entry had its :repo and :business-id fields updated, and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence. :optional-technologies was already empty and stays empty", :adr/candidate-8129-screened-first-and-deferred "'8129' (Other building and industrial cleaning activities), the natural low-friction sibling flagged in ADR-2607103900's own Alternatives section, was screened FIRST this build. grep -rli 'chimney|disinfection|decontaminat|industrial.clean|specialized.clean|window.clean' surfaced a genuine, direct overlap: cloud-itonami-unspsc-73 ('Independent Industrial Cleaning & Certification Robotics') already covers scheduled industrial equipment/facility cleaning with governed post-clean sensor certification for manufacturing plants and food/pharma facilities -- directly read and confirmed substantial overlap. Rather than force a narrow carve-out, '8129' was DEFERRED (not rejected) for future careful scoping, consistent with this fleet's established 'defer, don't force' discipline", :adr/twentysixth-spec-authoring-build "TWENTY-SIXTH 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-3312 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-3312 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 26, :spec 514, :total 646}", :adr/date "2026-07-10", :db/id -1, :adr/real-repo-naming-3312 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3312 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 131 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy C####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-C3312' to 'cloud-itonami-3312' to match", :adr/candidate-selection-3312 "'3312' (Repair of machinery) selected instead: scoped to diagnostic, overhaul and certified repair of EXISTING industrial equipment (pumps, compressors, turbines, manufacturing machinery), richly regulated (ASME 'R' stamp for authorized pressure-vessel/boiler repair in the US; EU Pressure Equipment Directive (PED)-compliant repair procedures; OEM certified-service-provider programs gating warranty validity on an authorized repair process), natural robotics-premise fit (diagnostic scanning, teardown/reassembly assist, non-destructive-testing inspection). grep -rli 'machinery.repair|industrial.equipment.repair|equipment.maintenance.and.repair' across the fleet returned completely empty. Distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-3020 and every other manufacturing vertical (which build NEW equipment) and from cloud-itonami-unspsc-73 (cleans/certifies contamination-free equipment, not functional repair) -- both directly confirmed non-redundant. Governor keyword :machinery-repair-governor grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C3312) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-3312 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDU